  "2026-11-10T18:08:44.418Z",codex-agent,"The single bounded full npm run exposed a separate scheduling defect in the existing pm-runner spawn-overlap test: first child finished before independent child started (observed order: start first, end first, start independent, start second, end independent, end second). Both commands succeeded and workspace serialization held; the overlap assertion relied on 120 ms being longer than independent process startup. Replacing that startup assumption with an explicit child-start handshake while retaining the delay, timeout, event-loop assertion, and ordering assertions. No retry, skip or timeout increase; full suite continues and its failed result will be reported. Auth 12/12 also passes in this full run, so its original CI failure is still unconfirmed."
  "2026-11-10T18:11:12.483Z",codex-agent,"Thread mapping for this continuation: PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61kDtM binds physical workspace/tracker identities, pins both queued SDK and CLI execution, and refuses reads after symlink switches; regression storage switches cannot escape authorized reads or queued SDK and CLI commands. PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61kM0_ compares installed Markdown using the actual pack inventory, with nested/mandatory/uppercase byte-mutation coverage. PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61kM1T parses CommonMark closing fences and strips unclosed fences to EOF. PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61kM1a reports malformed percent encodings as missing links instead of aborting. PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61kM1e separates unavailable Git revisions from missing files, verified in a real shallow clone lacking origin/main and an older commit. All five findings are valid and fixed; no thread replies or resolutions. The pack-receipt nitpick is also covered by malformed/empty receipt regressions."
  "2026-11-10T18:11:15.328Z",codex-agent,"Final focused follow-up: Node 22.23.4 pm-runner.test.ts passes 8/8 after replacing only the child-start scheduling assumption; test/scripts typecheck, lint and zero-duplication gate pass again. Expanded storage-switch regression passes 1/1 after all behavioral-revert functions are restored. Actual packed-artifact extraction audit passes: 513 packed files, 12 Markdown documents, all relative targets present and every installed Markdown byte equal to source. Artifact SHA-256 4e83a29464740bc2a48986728498df2119d9482217f4c4231981f68764e4c62a. This artifact audit certifies links/content, not installed npm/Bun host scenarios; full packed-consumer acceptance is still running."
  "2026-11-10T18:13:58.718Z",codex-agent,"Final bounded full-suite receipt: timeout 2700 npm test -- --test-concurrency=2 --test-reporter=tap, exact CI Node 22.23.4 with isolated HOME/Git identity, finished rather than timing out. Read results: 962 tests, 961 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped, 0 canceled, duration 1016680 ms. Sole failure was the pre-handshake spawn-overlap test already described; after that test-only correction, node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/pm-runner.test.ts passes 8/8. The full suite was not rerun, honoring the one-run budget, so final-head full certification remains for CI. Other evidence: pinned importer gate 97/97; restored read/document regressions 27/27; expanded storage-switch regression 1/1. npm run accept:packed passes 4/4 consumers (npm and native Bun; minimum host 2026.10.4 and current 2026.11.6), all eight launchers, and digest 4e83a29464740bc2a48986728498df2119d9482217f4c4231981f68764e4c62a. Typechecks, lint, build, 0% duplication, docstrings, strict tracker health, changelog generation/check, release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Committed dist rebuilt. Full coverage/capacity/release chains are delegated to CI under the continuation gate budget."
  "2026-11-10T18:13:59.947Z",codex-agent,"Auth CI investigation remains unresolved, not fixed: original head 90d41c7 passes all 12 auth tests locally on Node 24 and exact CI Node 22.23.4, and the original head also passes 12/12 under c8 with isolated HOME/Git identity. The updated full Node 22 suite passes all 12 auth tests as well. CI job 129639050619 reports 943 passed plus one file failure after 632 ms, with no auth subtest output and no rejection/after-hook/signal cause in the available log. That evidence does not prove a post-subtest failure. No speculative auth production change, skip, retry or timeout increase was made; a reproducing failure or raw worker/TAP exit diagnostics is still required to establish and fix that cause. All five requested review findings have behavioral fixes and recorded failing-before/passing-after proofs. Existing PR #305 and roadmap item reused; no second PR/item, hosted data, raw agent transcript, review reply or thread resolution. Leaving this item in progress for orchestrator verification and releasing only this continuation claim."
